cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Onera in your research, please cite it using the metadata below, along with MNE-Python and YASA."
title: "Onera: Interactive Sleep EEG Analysis Suite"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lupu
    given-names: Alexandru
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3320-7467"
    affiliation: "University of Fribourg, Switzerland"
abstract: >-
  Onera is an interactive Python (Marimo) suite for sleep EEG and
  polysomnography (PSG) staging and analysis, combining two complementary
  applications: Onera_SleepScorer.py for automated sleep staging with human-in-the-process through interactive hypnogram triage with pre-filtered waveform,
  multi-electrode soft-voting consensus, 
  inspection, and .Markers/.txt export; and Onera_PreAwakening.py for
  whole-night sleep macro-architecture and targeted pre-awakening EEG analysis
  including buffer-padded FIR filtering, automated artifact rejection, Welch
  PSD bandpower, scalp topographies, power-domain STFT spectrograms, and master
  CSV export.
keywords:
  - sleep
  - EEG
  - polysomnography
  - dreaming
  - serial awakenings
  - spectral analysis
  - hypnogram
  - spectrogram
  - sleep scoring
  - automated
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexandru-lupu-sci/Onera"
version: "1.0.0"
